  <!-- Citizen Cybersecurity & Identity Protection Advisory -->
  <section class="py-12 sm:py-16 border-t border-[var(--color-hairline)] bg-[var(--color-canvas-elevated)]">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-start">
        <div class="lg:col-span-7 space-y-4">
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-900 bg-amber-50 border border-amber-300 px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-[var(--radius-sm)] font-medium">
            <span>CONSUMER SECURITY DIRECTIVE</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)] tracking-tight">
            Protecting Your Digital Identity on Public Portals
          </h2>
          <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-body)] leading-relaxed">
            Because your SSO ID acts as the master key to your Jan Aadhaar bank subsidies, land ownership records, and recruitment exam admit cards, safeguarding your digital credentials is of paramount importance. Thousands of cybersecurity incidents in Rajasthan arise from citizens entering credentials on unauthorized third-party websites or failing to log out on public computers.
          </p>

          <div class="space-y-3 pt-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-[var(--color-body)]">
            <div class="p-3.5 bg-[var(--color-canvas)] border border-[var(--color-hairline)] rounded-[var(--radius-sm)] space-y-1">
              <span class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)] block">1. Verify the Official Domain URL Strictly</span>
              <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed">
                Always ensure your browser address bar displays <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">https://sso.rajasthan.gov.in</strong> before typing your username or password. Fraudulent phishing portals frequently purchase similar domains (such as <code>.com</code>, <code>.org</code>, or <code>.co.in</code> extensions) to steal user identities. Legitimate state portals exclusively end in <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">.gov.in</strong>.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="p-3.5 bg-[var(--color-canvas)] border border-[var(--color-hairline)] rounded-[var(--radius-sm)] space-y-1">
              <span class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)] block">2. Public Cyber Cafe &amp; e-Mitra Kiosk Precautions</span>
              <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed">
                If applying for government vacancies at an internet cafe, always open a <strong>Private / Incognito Window</strong>. Never allow the browser to save your password. After completing fee payment, manually click the <strong>"Log Out"</strong> icon at the top right and close the browser completely to purge session tokens.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="p-3.5 bg-[var(--color-canvas)] border border-[var(--color-hairline)] rounded-[var(--radius-sm)] space-y-1">
              <span class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)] block">3. Immediate Action on Suspicious SMS Alerts</span>
              <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed">
                If you receive an unsolicited SMS alert from <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">RJ-SSOGOV</strong> stating that an OTP was requested or that your password was updated, immediately log in to sso.rajasthan.gov.in, navigate to Profile Settings, update your password, and call the DoIT&amp;C helpdesk at <strong>0141-5153222</strong>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="lg:col-span-5 space-y-4">
          <div class="p-6 bg-[var(--color-canvas)] border border-[var(--color-hairline)] rounded-[var(--radius-md)] space-y-4 shadow-[0_1px_2px_rgba(0,0,0,0.02)]">
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">
              Digital Identity Checklist:
            </h3>
            <ul class="space-y-2.5 text-xs text-[var(--color-body)] list-disc pl-5">
              <li>Keep your mobile number synchronized in both Aadhaar and Jan Aadhaar cards.</li>
              <li>Never create a secondary SSO ID; merge existing duplicates to prevent recruitment rejection.</li>
              <li>Ensure your name and date of birth match your Class 10 mark sheet letter-for-letter.</li>
              <li>Keep your 1-time OTR transaction receipt saved securely in Google Drive or printed form.</li>
              <li>Change your SSO password every 90 days following strong complexity rules (minimum 8 characters with numbers and symbols).</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
